# Cloudflare Pages custom response headers.
# Docs: https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/
# Lives in the build output directory (wrangler.toml: pages_build_output_dir = "./").

# Cloudflare Pages' default for non-HTML assets is
# `Cache-Control: public, max-age=14400, must-revalidate`, which lets browsers
# reuse styles.css / script.js / products.js / photos for up to 4 hours without
# even revalidating. That is why visitors had to hard-refresh after a deploy:
# the HTML updated but the CSS/JS/images behind it did not.
#
# Force revalidation on every load instead. Unchanged assets come back as 304
# (empty body), so this is cheap; changed assets are picked up immediately.
# The ?v= query strings in the HTML are harmless redundancy on top of this.
#
# Note: _headers does not apply to Pages Functions responses (see docs), so the
# Stripe checkout function is unaffected.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
